{
  "about": "Recipe for the game's sound bank. tools/prepare-audio.py cuts these regions (seconds) out of the recordings in sources.json and writes assets/audio/bank/*.mp3 plus bank.json. loop: steady regions joined with crossfades and levelled, played by the seamless grain player. texture: a smooth bed built offline from many short overlapping grains of a rhythmic source (wading, mud). oneshots: the loudest separate events found in the regions. clip: one cut. Engine layers: hz is the firing frequency measured in the recording (rpm = hz * 120 / cylinders; `rpm` when it could not be measured), flatten [lo, hi] is the search band for following a rev sweep and resampling it to hz. on: part-throttle anchors by revs. pull: working hard. gears: top speed in km/h of each sound-only gear in H, sized to how fast the class's trucks really accelerate. holdS: the least time in seconds between sound-gear shifts.",
